WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.760
Stop skipping breakfast.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.580
Or, you should skip breakfast?

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.070
We've all heard that breakfast is the

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.660
most important meal of the day.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.420
But some actors and
athletes like Terry Crews

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.730
are adamant about not eating breakfast.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:14.870
So who's right?

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.290
Is breakfast good or bad?

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.110
I stopped eating breakfast
for two weeks to find out.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:23.300
I can't eat anything before
12, when I have lunch.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.490
For as long as I can remember,

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.290
I've had breakfast every single morning.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.260
But, I also know a lot of
people who don't eat breakfast.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.070
And that works great for them.

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.830
To be honest, I don't think
it's going to go very well

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:38.020
because I'll be awake from
six all the way until noon,

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:41.220
a full six hours without
eating a single thing.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.780
It's a lot different than what I'm used to

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.340
and it might be really
hard, especially at first.

00:00:45.607 --> 00:00:47.610
Half of you are probably typing a comment

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.460
about how you never eat breakfast.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.430
But making a change to your
daily routine isn't easy.

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.360
And I wanted to find out if my life

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.900
was better or worse without breakfast.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.170
Today was my first day
not eating breakfast.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.590
And I've got to say, it went pretty well.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:02.790
I was surprised to find out that

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.970
when I woke up, I wasn't that hungry.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:08.080
I made coffee, made lunch for the day,

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.130
and still wasn't feeling
like I needed breakfast.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.450
I stayed pretty busy.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:17.350
It was already noon and I had
barely craved any food at all.

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:18.260
I don't want to jinx it,

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.610
but I'm feeling pretty
optimistic for the week.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:23.950
So it's Wednesday.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.650
It's been three days of no breakfast.

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:29.740
And I've got to say, it's
getting a little bit harder.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:31.739
So yeah, it wasn't going well.

00:01:31.739 --> 00:01:35.361
I feel like every day around 10:30 or 11,

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.840
I get really hungry.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.480
My stomach starts to
growl and I start seeing

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.840
or smelling food around the
office that other people have.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.070
And it's a lot more challenging
than when I first wake up.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.890
And I know it's like okay,
that's not actually a problem.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:52.770
But if you're someone
who's trying to diet,

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:55.130
trying to eat less, trying to snack less,

00:01:55.130 --> 00:01:56.640
it can be really challenging when you have

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.610
a lot of options around the office

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:01.080
that can be really quick or convenient.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.460
I've actually amassed kind of a

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:04.720
large store of snacks at my desk,

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.433
all of the stuff I can't
eat until after lunch.

00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:10.160
And then I'm like "Oh,
you can't even eat that."

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.300
And it just kind of sits
there and stares back at me.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.120
I think I can make it through the week,

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.490
but I am a little worried
about the weekend.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.510
Waking up at 6 a.m. and not eating

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:21.130
until 12 is such a long time.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:22.710
Why do I need breakfast when so

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.550
many people can live without it?

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.430
What's actually going on here?

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:27.960
I spoke with Dr. Peterson,

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.953
a scientist at the University
of Alabama, to find out.

00:02:30.953 --> 00:02:32.659
So what I think has happened

00:02:32.659 --> 00:02:35.420
in breakfast skipping and why
it's so confusing is there's

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.970
actually not one way to
necessarily skip breakfast.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:42.100
You actually have better blood
sugar control in the morning

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.270
and you digest your food a
little faster in the morning,

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:45.670
as well as you burn very slightly

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.420
more calories when you eat in the morning.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.530
So all this evidence
kind of points towards

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:51.770
the morning as being optimal for eating.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.299
So if the morning is the
optimal time for eating,

00:02:54.299 --> 00:02:56.810
is skipping breakfast hurting me?

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.670
Was this whole challenge pointless?

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.520
On the flip side, we
have also learned over

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.050
the past decade that it looks like having

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:06.770
extended bouts of fasting
is good for your health.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.960
What's really interesting is
that you have hunger hormones.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.150
And these hunger hormones adapt to

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.570
whatever you usually do or to your habits.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.190
What this means in the short-term,

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.790
if you don't normally skip breakfast

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.800
and then you suddenly skip breakfast,

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.770
you have to overcome that inertia

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:23.770
of changing your hunger hormone patterns.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.400
Because your hunger hormone says "Okay,

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.170
well you usually eat breakfast.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.130
And now you're going to skip it,

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:29.280
so I'm going to make you very hungry."

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.580
Any time you have a regular
eating pattern and change that,

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.850
regardless of what
eating pattern you're on,

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.762
you will have an initial barrier
where it's quite difficult

00:03:37.762 --> 00:03:39.907
in the beginning and
then over time you adapt.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.590
Maybe my new routine is
worse than my old one.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.050
It's been about a week and a half.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:47.470
And I've gotta say, it's getting easier.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.810
I thought not having breakfast on

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:50.910
the weekend was going to be a nightmare.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.720
But it was actually a lot easier

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:55.530
because I woke up later and
didn't have as much time

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:59.960
between waking up and noon
as I do on the workday.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.260
But I do still miss breakfast.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.570
I just enjoy breakfast and
eating something in the morning.

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.480
Even if I'm not super hungry,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.930
I think I'll still miss that aspect.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.620
The whole thing has really made me

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:13.720
wonder how much breakfast matters.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.180
It kind of feels like
breakfast was just the routine.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:17.230
It was just my norm.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.300
So that's what I liked and
that's what I was used to.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.580
After a week and a half
of not eating breakfast,

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.320
it started to seem like I was finally

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.090
getting used to my new routine.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.208
Maybe I could turn into someone
who never eats breakfast.

00:04:29.208 --> 00:04:31.060
But I wouldn't count on it.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.840
It's finally Friday.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.170
And tomorrow I can have
breakfast once again.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.020
After two weeks, I've
realized that I can go

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.460
without eating breakfast
and still survive.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:42.680
But I miss breakfast.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:44.954
Not eating before 12 was really tough,

00:04:44.954 --> 00:04:47.460
especially with all the
food around the office.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.000
And it definitely brought down
my mood throughout the day.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.222
But I never really felt a
big change in my productivity

00:04:53.222 --> 00:04:56.890
or even my energy levels
before or after lunch.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:59.220
And my weight stayed pretty much the same.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:02.540
Breakfast isn't bad for you,
but it's also not essential.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:03.650
You should do what fits best for

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.730
your dietary needs and your routine.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.020
I no longer feel helpless
without breakfast

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:09.910
and I'm able to create a routine

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.770
that fits my schedule and my daily needs.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:14.220
Before I started this challenge,

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:17.610
I loved breakfast and I thought
I needed it to start my day.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.640
Now I don't really feel that way.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.430
I still like breakfast and
will continue to eat it,

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:25.520
but I don't feel that reliance
on it like I used to have.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.650
So it turns out you can skip breakfast.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.310
But Dr. Peterson pointed out that

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:30.690
instead of skipping breakfast,

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:32.030
it's better to shorten the window

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.700
of time for meals each day.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.070
Two broad types of meal timing approaches

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:37.960
that we have found to be beneficial.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.560
One is the daily
intermittent fasting approach

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:42.680
where you're eating in
a narrow time period.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.770
And it looks like probably
eating in the middle of the day,

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:49.690
say from 10 a.m. to 6 p.m.
is also good for your health.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.760
There is a lot of evidence
that even if you can't

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:54.530
change the timing of
breakfast, lunch, and dinner,

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:57.340
if you at least make your
largest meals earlier,

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:59.040
be breakfast and or lunch,

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.255
that you can still get a
lot of benefits from that.

00:06:01.255 --> 00:06:03.750
Some people love eating breakfast.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.090
And good for them.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.070
But don't let someone try and tell you

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:09.890
that you're throwing the day
away if you skip breakfast.

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:11.367
The most important meal of the day

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:12.774
depends on who's eating it.

00:06:14.132 --> 00:06:17.132
Now this is how breakfast should be.

